# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the working tree as well as in the object
# store.
#
# Not a style preference. `xtask/section9-gate-table.json` is a GENERATED
# artifact whose test asserts that regenerating it "must reproduce it byte for
# byte", and `gate --audit` FAILS when it disagrees with §9. Git's default
# `core.autocrlf` on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, so the file the
# generator produced and the file the test read back differed by a byte per
# line — and the whole point of that artifact is that they cannot.
#
# Found by the first native Windows CI run of this repository: everything else
# was green and this failed with
# `left: "{\n  \"row_count\"...` / `right: "{\r\n  \"row_count\"...`.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git normalise on commit; `eol=lf` is what stops the
# checkout from undoing it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the artifacts whose byte-identity is asserted, so a future
# narrowing of the line above cannot quietly reintroduce this.
*.json  text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.rs    text eol=lf
